    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "RENTER RESPONSIBILITIES AND RULES",
      "level": 2,
      "style": "SH"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "Renter must have a valid driver's license appropriate for the Vehicle type. If the Vehicle is a large RV, Renter may need a special license depending on state law and Vehicle weight.",
        "Renter must be at least {{minimum_age}} years old and must not be intoxicated or under the influence of drugs or alcohol while operating the Vehicle.",
        "Renter is responsible for the Vehicle from the time of pickup until the time of return, including all damage, loss, theft, fines, tickets, and accidents.",
        "Renter must not drive the Vehicle outside of {{allowed_geographic_area}} without Owner's written consent.",
        "Renter must not use the Vehicle for any illegal purpose, towing of other vehicles (unless equipped and approved), off-road driving, racing, or any purpose not consistent with the Vehicle's intended recreational use.",
        "Renter must not allow any person not listed on the agreement to drive the Vehicle.",
        "Renter must not smoke inside the Vehicle. Smoking damage is not covered by insurance and will be charged to Renter.",
        "Renter must not have pets in the Vehicle unless approved by Owner in writing. Pet damage will be charged to Renter.",
        "Renter must not leave the Vehicle unattended with the keys in it or with any person not authorized to have them.",
        "Renter must follow all manufacturer instructions and safety guidelines for the Vehicle, including proper hookup of utilities (electricity, water, sewer, propane), leveling, and use of all systems.",
        "Renter is responsible for proper disposal of waste (gray water, black water, trash) at approved dump stations.",
        "Renter must not modify, tamper with, or remove any equipment, accessories, or systems of the Vehicle.",
        "Renter must maintain adequate propane, fuel, and battery levels during the rental period.",
        "Renter must check and maintain appropriate tire pressure and perform pre-trip and post-trip inspections.",
        "Renter must report any accidents, incidents, or mechanical issues to Owner immediately.",
        "{{renter_rules_extra}}"
      ]
    },
